{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "The Good Old Days"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Work Hard, Play Hard"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify and describe events in a range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " The Present Perfect Tense vs The Simple Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about an action or event that is connected to the present in some way. <br><br>You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event <span class=\"strong\">not</span> connected to the present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is common to mix both the Simple Past and Present Perfect when you talk about differences between the past and present."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you can use the Present Perfect there is a connection between what happened in the past and now. You use time markers like <span class=\"italic\">for</span>, <span class=\"italic\">just</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ever</span>, <span class=\"italic\">during</span>, with the Present Perfect."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you can use the Simple Past the time is always past. You use time markers connected with the past like:  <span class=\"italic\">then</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ago</span>, <span class=\"italic\">yesterday</span>, <span class=\"italic\">when I was \u2026 </span> with the Simple Past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What has it been like working for Google? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I went in to Google with my own expectations. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "One thing I've grown to appreciate is the amazing food."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Adjectives About Feelings and Reactions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You talk about feelings and reactions using adjectives.  It is important to use the correct kind of adjective - it is common for English language learners to confuse the two kinds of adjectives when talking about feelings and reactions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. -ed adjectives<br/><br/>Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\"> -ed </span> are used to describe how a person <span class=\"strong\"> feels </span>, like <span class=\"italic\">annoyed </span>, <span class=\"italic\"> fascinated </span>, <span class=\"italic\"> entertained </span>, <span class=\"italic\"> surprised </span>, <span class=\"italic\"> worried </span> or <span class=\"italic\"> tired </span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">I feel relaxed.<br/>She comes reinvigorated.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "2. -ing adjectives"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Adjectives that end in <span class=\"strong\"> -ing </span> are used to describe things and situations</span>, like <span class=\"italic\">annoying</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> entertaining</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> surprising</span>, <span class=\"italic\"> worrying</span> or <span class=\"italic\">tiring</span>. These adjectives describe the <span class=\"strong\"> effect</span> something has on a person.\u2003"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Working at Google is interesting.</span> (It makes me feel interested).<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Work is sometimes surprising, too.</span> (It makes me feel surprised)."}, {"type": "example", "content": " She always comes out of her office reinvigorated and relaxed. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Working for Google is interesting."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "insightful "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "showing a deep understanding"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Working at Google has been insightful."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about work and play."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "impactful"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having a major effect on someone  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Working at Google has been impactful."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn7le08ob09aud02"}